e not given — they must be deduced from the surviving pixels by finding the axes that best preserve the existing symmetry.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/eval/seed397419310/5/codegen_prompts/2.codex.log:2636:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:258:(canonical dr == dc), so it reflects cleanly across all four corner orientations.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/eval/seed397419310/5/codegen_prompts/2.codex.log:2637:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/1/prompt.md:273:- Rotate the sprite (0/90/180/270°) so its contact edge has exactly N-2 contiguous cells aligned with the hub side, and the rotated sprite is mirror-symmetric along the contact-edge axis (UD for left/right, LR for top/bottom).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/eval/seed397419310/5/codegen_prompts/2.codex.log:2661:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/3/prompt.md:39:- Monochrome components become solid Manhattan stripes between mapped endpoints.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/eval/seed397419310/5/codegen_prompts/2.codex.log:2662:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/3/prompt.md:48:Clean each color layer by enforcing vertical mirror symmetry.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/eval/seed397419310/5/codegen_prompts/2.codex.log:2663:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/3/prompt.md:56:- Remove any pixel that lacks a same-color mirror counterpart across that axis.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/eval/seed397419310/5/codegen_prompts/2.codex.log:2664:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/3/prompt.md:192:Reveal the rectangular patch hidden by the solid marker using the grid's reflection symmetries.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/eval/seed397419310/5/codegen_prompts/2.codex.log:2665:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/3/prompt.md:196:- The visible pattern has horizontal and vertical reflection symmetry on a large lower/right strip.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/eval/seed397419310/5/codegen_prompts/2.codex.log:2666:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/3/prompt.md:197:- The top and left outer